{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPE1n1sTezxSLBuuQp9opH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-571\"\n3\ttitle = \"The snapshot copies only what the act authorises: copy_live scoped to the flipped registry and the named --approves refs\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"medium\"\n7\tpriority = 5\n8\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n9\t+++\n10\t\n11\t## Deliverable\n12\t\n13\t`baseline_snapshot.copy_live` is scoped to the act. A refresh of a populated\n14\tsnapshot now copies ONLY the registries the act authorises — every registry a\n15\t`--approves` ref names, plus every registry an approving `Status` move happened\n16\tin (`_authorised_registries`: a flip on an existing row, or a new row that\n17\tarrives already `Approved`) — and leaves every other registry byte-identical to\n18\twhat it was. The seed / first-signing (a `--seed`, a scaffold that still holds\n19\tno registry, or an unreadable record being repaired — decided by\n20\t`_refresh_targets`) still copies the whole tree. Both mirror rules stay green\n21\tuntouched, because each is pinned to the file it judges:\n22\t`staged_snapshot_findings` only checks snapshot files IN the commit, and\n23\t`committed_snapshot_findings` compares each to live at its own writing commit —\n24\tan untouched file is not \"written\". This closes the whole-tree re-seal that\n25\tdragged live off-spine drift into the record on every spine-only approval.\n26\t\n27\t`--approves` is a NAMED list: `parse_approves` turns a `;`-joined `REGISTRY=REF`\n28\tCLI value into `{registry rel: ref}` (`resolve_registry` accepts a rel,\n29\tfilename, or carrier-less stem), and a ref mutes `refresh_refusal` for the ONE\n30\tregistry it names — the secondary widening (`if approves: return \"\"` muted all\n31\tseven) is closed. `_record_approval` records the act's scope into the prose\n32\tstamp: the registries copied and, for each, whether a ref named it or a Status\n33\tmove authorised it. `intake.py snapshot`'s `--approves` help/metavar move to\n34\t`REGISTRY=REF`; parsing lives in `baseline_snapshot`, so intake grows by the\n35\ttwo-line CLI edge only (reviewed baseline bump 1177→1179, recorded in the\n36\tratchet with reason in the fragment).\n37\t\n38\tTests: `tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py` gains four scope tests (a spine flip\n39\tleaves off-spine snapshot bytes untouched and the census intact; a named ref\n40\tcopies exactly its registry; a ref mutes only the registry it names; the seed\n41\tstill copies all) and a mirror-green-across-a-scoped-act test; the two existing\n42\ttests whose contract changed (a traced-only and a Drafted-only refresh now copy\n43\tNOTHING rather than the whole tree) and the approval-stamp test (exercised via a\n44\tnamed amendment, since a traced-only refresh now writes nothing) are re-pointed;\n45\t`tests/test_trace_briefs.py`'s two `--approves` callers move to the named form.\n46\tFull-suite result and the pre-existing-failure accounting are in the fragment\n47\t`docs/log.d/WI-571-snapshot-copy-scope.md`.\n48\t\n49\tNOT done here (plan §2): `OI-78` is not ruled — rows already absorbed at\n50\t`580df781` stay absorbed until the owner rules; this row stops the NEXT act from\n51\tabsorbing more. The queued reseal row `WI-569`'s `## Context` is updated (triage)\n52\tto record that its regeneration now re-seals only the spine rows and leaves the\n53\toff-spine census to its own review. No spine rows were minted or re-statused, so\n54\tno approval brief regeneration was owed. Standing constraint honoured: no\n55\t`Status` flip, no `intake.py snapshot` run against this repo's own snapshot —\n56\tthe scoped copy was driven on scratch scaffolds and tmp trees only.\n57\t\n58\t## Context\n59\t\n60\tFiled 2026-09-01 (evening supervised session) from the owner's question on OI-78 and an independent investigation: baseline_snapshot.copy_live mirrors all seven registries on every intake.py snapshot act, so a spine Status flip re-seals whatever off-spine drift is live at that moment (9 of 21 prior snapshot commits did; the wi508 handback merge was not causal). Scope copy_live to the flipped registry plus the registries named by --approves; make --approves a named list; stamp the act's scope; re-read the queued reseal row's stand branch. Read the plan's section 2 before widening - moving the write to the trunk lane is the recorded alternative, not this row.\n61\t\n62\t**Standing constraint (owner ruling 2026-09-01, the approval act is the\n63\tadjudicator's):** if this row authors or amends spine rows (SR/LLR/TC), leave\n64\tthem `Drafted`; do NOT flip any `Status`, and do NOT run `intake.py snapshot`\n65\tor write `docs/archive/last_approved/` on this lane — including while testing\n66\tthe scoped copy, which must be driven on a scaffold, never on this repo's\n67\tsnapshot. The flip and the snapshot are performed on trunk by the\n68\tadjudication arm once it ships.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c514bde5-8ba9-45d3-97fd-4ef59ca4534d","uuid":"9b174b0d-a879-4f96-8ab2-de613f095914","timestamp":"2026-09-02T03:05:15.027Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-571-the-snapshot-copies-only-what/docs/work/complete/WI-571-the-snapshot-copies-only-what.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-571\"\ntitle = \"The snapshot copies only what the act authorises: copy_live scoped to the flipped registry and the named --approves refs\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nspecref = \"\"\nbuildtier = \"medium\"\npriority = 5\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n+++\n\n## Deliverable\n\n`baseline_snapshot.copy_live` is scoped to the act. A refresh of a populated\nsnapshot now copies ONLY the registries the act authorises — every registry a\n`--approves` ref names, plus every registry an approving `Status` move happened\nin (`_authorised_registries`: a flip on an existing row, or a new row that\narrives already `Approved`) — and leaves every other registry byte-identical to\nwhat it was. The seed / first-signing (a `--seed`, a scaffold that still holds\nno registry, or an unreadable record being repaired — decided by\n`_refresh_targets`) still copies the whole tree. Both mirror rules stay green\nuntouched, because each is pinned to the file it judges:\n`staged_snapshot_findings` only checks snapshot files IN the commit, and\n`committed_snapshot_findings` compares each to live at its own writing commit —\nan untouched file is not \"written\". This closes the whole-tree re-seal that\ndragged live off-spine drift into the record on every spine-only approval.\n\n`--approves` is a NAMED list: `parse_approves` turns a `;`-joined `REGISTRY=REF`\nCLI value into `{registry rel: ref}` (`resolve_registry` accepts a rel,\nfilename, or carrier-less stem), and a ref mutes `refresh_refusal` for the ONE\nregistry it names — the secondary widening (`if approves: return \"\"` muted all\nseven) is closed. `_record_approval` records the act's scope into the prose\nstamp: the registries copied and, for each, whether a ref named it or a Status\nmove authorised it. `intake.py snapshot`'s `--approves` help/metavar move to\n`REGISTRY=REF`; parsing lives in `baseline_snapshot`, so intake grows by the\ntwo-line CLI edge only (reviewed baseline bump 1177→1179, recorded in the\nratchet with reason in the fragment).\n\nTests: `tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py` gains four scope tests (a spine flip\nleaves off-spine snapshot bytes untouched and the census intact; a named ref\ncopies exactly its registry; a ref mutes only the registry it names; the seed\nstill copies all) and a mirror-green-across-a-scoped-act test; the two existing\ntests whose contract changed (a traced-only and a Drafted-only refresh now copy\nNOTHING rather than the whole tree) and the approval-stamp test (exercised via a\nnamed amendment, since a traced-only refresh now writes nothing) are re-pointed;\n`tests/test_trace_briefs.py`'s two `--approves` callers move to the named form.\nFull-suite result and the pre-existing-failure accounting are in the fragment\n`docs/log.d/WI-571-snapshot-copy-scope.md`.\n\nNOT done here (plan §2): `OI-78` is not ruled — rows already absorbed at\n`580df781` stay absorbed until the owner rules; this row stops the NEXT act from\nabsorbing more. The queued reseal row `WI-569`'s `## Context` is updated (triage)\nto record that its regeneration now re-seals only the spine rows and leaves the\noff-spine census to its own review. No spine rows were minted or re-statused, so\nno approval brief regeneration was owed. Standing constraint honoured: no\n`Status` flip, no `intake.py snapshot` run against this repo's own snapshot —\nthe scoped copy was driven on scratch scaffolds and tmp trees only.\n\n## Context\n\nFiled 2026-09-01 (evening supervised session) from the owner's question on OI-78 and an independent investigation: baseline_snapshot.copy_live mirrors all seven registries on every intake.py snapshot act, so a spine Status flip re-seals whatever off-spine drift is live at that moment (9 of 21 prior snapshot commits did; the wi508 handback merge was not causal). Scope copy_live to the flipped registry plus the registries named by --approves; make --approves a named list; stamp the act's scope; re-read the queued reseal row's stand branch. Read the plan's section 2 before widening - moving the write to the trunk lane is the recorded alternative, not this row.\n\n**Standing constraint (owner ruling 2026-09-01, the approval act is the\nadjudicator's):** if this row authors or amends spine rows (SR/LLR/TC), leave\nthem `Drafted`; do NOT flip any `Status`, and do NOT run `intake.py snapshot`\nor write `docs/archive/last_approved/` on this lane — including while testing\nthe scoped copy, which must be driven on a scaffold, never on this repo's\nsnapshot. The flip and the snapshot are performed on trunk by the\nadjudication arm once it ships.\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
