{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cedt9JyvrLGGCEHjheyT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both rework findings are addressed, committed, and the row is fully closed. Working tree is clean.\n\n## Summary\n\nI addressed both MINOR findings from review A (`002-REVIEW-A-61180ab.md`, CHANGES-REQUESTED) on WI-571.\n\n**Finding 1 — Status-move refreshes went unstamped** (`baseline_snapshot.py`)\n`copy_live` recorded the approval stamp only `if approves:`, so a refresh authorised by a `Status` move alone copied its registry but wrote no prose stamp — leaving that approval unauditable, contrary to the contract the Deliverable promises. Fix:\n- `_refresh_targets` now returns `(targets, first_signing)`.\n- `copy_live` stamps **every non-seed refresh that copied a registry**, passing `approves or {}` so the per-registry reason reads `Status move` when no ref named it. The seed and a copy-nothing (traced-only) refresh still write no line.\n- Updated the README prose and the two docstrings to match.\n- New red→green test `test_a_STATUS_MOVE_refresh_is_STAMPED_as_a_Status_move`.\n\n**Finding 2 — WI-569 triage claimed a bare snapshot would copy the LLR rows** (`WI-569` queued spec)\nThe triage asserted WI-569's approval commit *flips* LLR-203/LLR-204, but the same spec states both are already `Approved` (the KEPT `580df781` flip) and merely confirmed — so under the scoped copy a bare `intake.py snapshot` moves no `Status` and copies **zero** registries. Corrected the triage: a bare run copies nothing (the LLR rows are already sealed byte-identical, so no spine reseal is needed); to re-seal any registry deliberately the row must **name** it with `--approves`. Reconciled the matching Deliverable sentence and test count.\n\n**Verification**\n- Targeted suites: `112 passed` (baseline_snapshot, complexity/module ratchets, trace_briefs, intake).\n- Commit bar: smoke `1452 passed`, wall **22.8s < 60s** budget. The sole smoke failure is the pre-existing drained-tree `test_wi_convert` issue already documented in the log fragment (`docs/work/cancelled/README.md` redirect stub) — not this WI's, verified identical at trunk.\n- Zero new ruff findings introduced (the remaining `.format()`→f-string suggestions are pre-existing file style).\n\n**Close state**: spec in `docs/work/complete/`, `specref = \"\"`, Deliverable filled before Context, log fragment updated with a rework section. No spine rows minted/re-statused, so no approval brief was owed. Final commit `0e12c518` carries the `WI: WI-571` trailer."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1522,"cache_read_input_tokens":103818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1522},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c514bde5-8ba9-45d3-97fd-4ef59ca4534d","uuid":"e41bb8e5-258e-4018-8cd2-635746760596","request_id":"req_011Cedt9J4caxJ2WBYxupkLT"}
